  "staffPermissionsSafetyChecklist": [
    "Create no staff role through onboarding; manually assign least-privilege staff permissions only to named, trusted staff.",
    "Keep private staff channels hidden from @everyone and all cosmetic/member roles; verify owner/staff access separately.",
    "Keep the five writable default discussion channels open to members; keep welcome and announcements read-only for members.",
    "Limit @everyone/@here mentions to trusted staff and avoid mass pings in setup/content posts.",
    "Enable and review Discord AutoMod/raid-protection safeguards appropriate to the server's current size; test false positives and maintain a human review path.",
    "Give public feedback forums clear templates and expectations; do not promise private ticket automation, response times, bug fixes, or roadmap commitments unless those exist.",
    "Use staff-only forum status tags only when the status is accurate; grant forum moderators Manage Threads only where needed.",
    "Keep notifications unassigned until a member opts in; test onboarding preview and answer-to-role/channel mapping before publishing."
  ],
